The current API uses an object definition passed to `pi.registerTool()`—not positional arguments ([official Pi docs](https://pi.dev/docs/latest/extensions#custom-tools)):

```ts
import type { ExtensionAPI } from "@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent";
import { Type } from "typebox";

export default function (pi: ExtensionAPI) {
  pi.registerTool({
    name: "my_tool",
    label: "My Tool",
    description: "What the tool does",
    parameters: Type.Object({
      input: Type.String(),
    }),

    async execute(toolCallId, params, signal, onUpdate, ctx) {
      return {
        content: [{ type: "text", text: `Received ${params.input}` }],
        details: {},
      };
    },
  });
}
```

The callback’s typed shape is:

```ts
execute(
  toolCallId: string,
  params: Static<TParams>,
  signal: AbortSignal | undefined,
  onUpdate: AgentToolUpdateCallback<TDetails> | undefined,
  ctx: ExtensionContext,
): Promise<AgentToolResult<TDetails>>
```

`onUpdate` has the shape:

```ts
(partialResult: AgentToolResult<TDetails>) => void
```

`content` is sent back to the LLM; `details` is arbitrary structured data for rendering or state. Throw from `execute()` to report failure (`isError: true`), as documented in the [custom-tool API reference](https://pi.dev/docs/latest/extensions#pi-registertool-definition).

